Krita Nova 28 - fingers work on the canvas right after the pen is lifted

Palm rejection (patch 09) kept ignoring touch on the canvas for 500 ms after
the pen was last used, and for as long as the pen hovered over the screen -
which it does right after a stroke. So the first finger touch after lifting
the pen (to pan, zoom or undo with a gesture) did nothing.

1. Hovering blocks touch only while the pen approaches the screen: from
   entering proximity (or, where the platform sends no proximity events, a
   hover move after 400 ms of pen silence) until its first press. After a
   release, a hovering pen no longer blocks touch.
2. The delay after lifting the pen is now 100 ms by default, under a new
   setting "palmRejectionLiftDelay" (Configure Krita > General > Tools,
   "Keep ignoring touch after the pen is lifted for"); the old 500 ms value
   saved as "palmRejectionDelay" is no longer used.
3. While the pen is down, and for touches the size of a palm, nothing
   changes.
